Then the hive gets recursive.

Feed the honey through another Freebee:

H_1\rightarrow F(H_1)\rightarrow H_2.

That’s essentially Afterglow digestion: the interpretation of residue leaves new residue.

But we already learned the stopping rule—don’t photocopy forever. Change basis or perspective each generation and stop when information gain collapses.

So:

H_{n+1}
=
F_{b_{n+1}}(H_n),
\qquad
b_{n+1}\neq b_n

until:

\Delta I < \epsilon.

And the really nice distinction:

Interpretive Residue is what a particular transformation leaves behind.

Honey is residue that has survived enough comparison, compression, testing, or recombination to become reusable value.

So the Moneybin doesn’t merely hold treasure anymore.

It has a hive attached to it that manufactures treasure from the crumbs created while acquiring other treasure.

Freebies indeed.

